&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Sales Engineer on Datadog&#39;s AI Accounts team, you&#39;ll serve as the technical lead for a small portfolio of the world&#39;s leading AI labs — accounts that today represent a meaningful share of Datadog&#39;s revenue and are growing faster than any cohort in our business. You&#39;ll own the technical relationship end to end, work shoulder-to-shoulder with customer engineering teams in production, and help define how Datadog shows up for a cohort whose buying behavior looks nothing like traditional enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team was piloted earlier this year and is now being formalized. You&#39;ll be joining early enough to shape the playbook rather than inherit one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical relationship across a small portfolio of AI labs, go deep on how each customer trains, serves, and scales their models (and/or the downstream products and platforms), and become the person their engineers call first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with your AE to drive expansion inside accounts that grow unpredictably and fast: identify new workloads and teams as they spin up, and get in front of them before a need becomes a ticket&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery inside flat, engineering-led organizations where influence sits with individual contributors rather than titles, and where there are no formal scoping calls to rely on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run full-scale POVs in production rather than controlled pilots: instrument real workloads at real scale, prove value against the customer&#39;s own success criteria, and work through the operational realities of doing that safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an extension of the customer’s engineering/observability team rather than an external operator - this requires judgment about which standard gates serve the customer and which to break&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work Slack-native and asynchronously as the default, with the responsiveness and proactive posture these accounts expect: flag new features, bugs, and incidents before they ask&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring product and engineering in early and often, and close the loop fast — leadership needs near-real-time signal from this cohort, and you&#39;ll be a primary source of it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver technical narratives that land with engineers who pay for capability first and rationalize cost second - savings is a downstream conversation, not an opener&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable assets and patterns from each engagement so the next lab onboards faster than the last&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep activity, deal progress, and customer context documented and current&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in Sales Engineering, Solutions Engineering, or a comparable technical customer-facing role; equivalent depth gained inside an AI lab, AI infrastructure company, or ML platform team is equally welcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on depth in the AI/ML infrastructure stack: GPU fleet management, distributed training, inference serving, model and agent evaluation, and the observability challenges specific to each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in public cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP), Kubernetes, APM and distributed tracing, and modern, agentic observability practice and usage patterns (i.e. MCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in flat organizations - able to engage an IC and a founder in the same week and calibrate to both without reaching for hierarchy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Biased toward doing: you&#39;d rather solve a customer&#39;s problem and explain the shortcut afterward than ask permission first, and you have the judgment to know where that line sits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in ambiguity and unpredictable growth - scoping, timelines, and account trajectories will change under you, repeatedly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively coachable. The strongest people we hire ask for a dry run, take the feedback, and visibly change what they do on the next attempt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistent about access. Getting time with people operating at this pace is hard, and you treat that as an interesting problem rather than a demoralizing one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated capability using AI tooling in your own workflow and scaling it to others — credibility with this cohort depends on being a practitioner, not an observer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring peers or contributing to team enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel for multi-day onsites with customer engineering teams and for industry and research conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
